      "body": "## Purpose\n\nA beam search request with a large `length_penalty` returns a 500 error. `get_beam_search_score` divides by `max(seq_len, 1) ** length_penalty`:\n\n- A large negative penalty underflows that to `0.0`, which raises `ZeroDivisionError: float division by zero`.\n- A large positive one raises `OverflowError`.\n\nBoth happen while sorting beams, after generation has already run. The schemathesis test on main (`test_openapi_stateless[POST /v1/chat/completions]`, build 91958) found it:\n\n```\nvllm/entrypoints/generate/beam_search/online.py:196 beam_search\n  -> utils.py:159 sort_beams_key -> utils.py:154 get_beam_search_score\nZeroDivisionError: float division by zero\n```\n\nThe `max(seq_len, 1)` guard from #56249 covers a zero length but not an extreme exponent.\n\n## Change\n\n- `get_beam_search_score` saturates instead of raising. An overflowed denominator gives a score of about 0. An underflowed one gives `-inf`, or `0.0` when the log-prob is 0. Beam order still follows the score everywhere it's finite.\n- `BeamSearchParams` rejects a non-finite `length_penalty` (`inf`/`nan`) with a `VLLMValidationError`, next to the existing `beam_width` check, so the API returns 400.\n\nThis isn't a duplicate: I searched open PRs for `length_penalty`, `get_beam_search_score` and beam-search ZeroDivisionError, and found nothing related.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nRun on h200-0 in the CI image for main `deb148e7`, with the changed files mounted:\n\n- `pytest tests/test_request_input_bounds.py`: 43 passed. The 4 new cases fail without the change.\n- `pre-commit` on the changed files (ruff, mypy-3.10): passed.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nClaude Code wrote this change and the tests, from the CI failure log, and ran the checks above. @khluu has not reviewed it yet; per AGENTS.md, he needs to review every line before it merges.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
